# Copy to .env (git-ignored) for scripts/refresh_and_deploy.sh and local cron.
#
# Recommended — one-time browser login, then headless refresh-token redeem (no daily paste):
#   ./scripts/setup_kiosk_browser.sh
#   ./scripts/refresh_and_deploy.sh
# Keep the refresh token warm (avoids weekly re-login). Also remints the flags
# table SAS from the current storage account key (survives key rotations):
#   crontab -e
#   15 */6 * * *  /Users/YOU/Code/paper-networks-audit/scripts/kiosk_keepalive.sh >> /tmp/kiosk-keepalive.log 2>&1
#   20 * * * *    /Users/YOU/Code/paper-networks-audit/scripts/refresh_flags_sas.sh >> /tmp/flags-sas-refresh.log 2>&1
# Profile: ~/.cache/frontiers-kiosk/chromium-profile/
#
# Forever-unattended (no personal SSO): ask IT for a Kiosk API service principal.
#
# Fallback — manual bearer (CI / if browser profile breaks):
# KIOSK_BEARER_TOKEN='eyJ...'   # kiosk-ui → DevTools → Authorization header
#
# Fallback — paste full connection string (expires ~24h):
# AUDIT_DB_CS='Server=...;Database=service-aira;User Id=KioskTemp_...;Password=...'
#
# Optional — bake manufactured-article flags into the snapshot:
# AUDIT_TABLE_CONN='DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=...;AccountKey=...'
